Migration 063 rebuilt conversation_request_kind, conversation_requests,
conversation_metrics_for and conversation_rollups so a side call was
classified by harness binding rather than thread shape.

Every one of those is declarative state, declared in
27_conversation_requests.sql and re-established on each boot, so the
migration's only lasting effect was on databases it had already reached.

It cannot be replayed. Its view tested `ai_request_payloads.offered_tools`,
which core 0.59.0 replaces with `offered_tools_sha256` (core migration
ai/033), so the current installer failed every upgrade from 0.52.0 at
"column p.offered_tools does not exist". The declarative file already reads
the digest column.

Retain the spent slot and existing tracking rows; never reuse this number.
